Known limitation carried into this patch (see /tmp/fj-vue-pager-20260928-result.md for detail):
under a real Storage.setItem failure (private-browsing policies), this module's own storage-
resilience shim (dashboard-pagination.mjs's private `memoryStore`/`failedRealWrites`) is a
separate in-memory instance from src/pagination.mjs's own equivalent private shim — each widget
type's in-memory fallback is independent. Under normal (non-throwing) Storage this is inert (both
read/write the same real Storage keys and behave identically); it only diverges if a classic
Fomantic pager and this Vue pager are both mounted in the same page load AND a real write throws,
in which case each independently re-reveals/re-bumps the shared habit counter once instead of
observing the other's already-set flag. Fix requires relocating the shim into pagination-model.mjs
(shared, not owned by this branch) so both widgets share one mirror; flagged for the file owner
rather than duplicated further or edited out-of-scope here.
